  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "n0ruwjpKRVRL3YF3p2WN9J675/Y=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T08:46:00.730Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "`addons/mail/security/ir.model.access.csv` grants `base.group_user` the permission tuple `1,1,1,1` on `model_mail_message` \u2014 read, write, create and unlink. `base.group_user` is every internal employee, not an administrative group. `mail.tracking.value.mail_message_id` is declared `ondelete='cascade'`, so removing the message silently takes the field-level diffs with it.\n\n`mail.message.unlink()` is an ordinary model method gated only by `check_access('unlink')`, which that ACL satisfies. Three documented context switches \u2014 `tracking_disable`, `mail_notrack` and a blessed `bypass_audit` token \u2014 provide further ways past tracking, and `account.lock_exception` is a first-class bypass model whose `reason` is nullable, which applies to everyone when `user_id` is null and never expires when `end_datetime` is null.\n\nWorth stating in Odoo's favour: editing is blocked \u2014 *\"Messages with tracking values cannot be modified\"* \u2014 and there is no automatic pruning of `mail.message`. The weakness is deletion by ordinary users, not mutation or drift.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-20T08:46:00.730443Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T08:46:00.730448Z"
    }
  },
